export anchor SerifProfessionalStyle:
    number: 204
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Serif professional
    idea: A calm report-like workspace where a modern serif carries headings and every figure, a plain sans carries the interface, and ruled lines replace cards.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #fbfaf7, the page background
        surface: #ffffff, the masthead, fields and swatch cards
        ink: #1f2430, text, heavy rules and progress fills
        muted: #5a5f6b, labels, meta lines and captions
        rule: #dcd8cf, hairlines between rows, never text
        navy: #23407a, the primary button, links, focus and this week bars
        mist: #b9c3d6, last week bars, never text
        pine: #1e6b47, On track with a filled circle
        ochre: #8a5300, At risk with a filled triangle
        brick: #a3262a, Behind with a crossed square and the overdue count
    type:
        Two stacks. Headings, project names and every figure use Charter,
        Bitstream Charter, Sitka Text, Cambria, Georgia, serif with lining
        tabular numerals. The interface uses system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto,
        Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif. KPI figures are 44px serif
        regular, the greeting 40px serif regular, the lede 19px serif in
        muted ink, section titles 22px serif semibold, project names 18px
        serif semibold, body 15px sans, meta 13px sans and the dateline 13px
        sans capitals tracked 0.08em.
    layout:
        A white masthead holds the serif brand, a search field, the New
        project button, a square bell and the user, with the six nav links
        as a text row underneath where Home has a 2px ink underline. The
        content is one centred column up to 1200px. A caps dateline, the
        serif greeting and a serif lede naming the 4 overdue tasks in brick
        open the page. The four KPIs sit in one ruled row with a 2px ink
        rule above, a hairline below and hairline dividers, no boxes, each
        with a small label, a big serif figure and a note. Below, two
        columns at about 1.75 to 1. The left holds Projects as a ruled
        list, each row with the serif name and team and task count, a thin
        ink progress bar with its percent, and the status word with its
        due date. The right holds Tasks completed with three serif totals
        and a two tone bar chart, then Recent activity as a ruled list with
        task names in serif italics. Below 900px the columns stack and the
        KPIs become two by two. On phones the search drops to its own row
        and each project row puts its progress bar under the name.
    spacing: An 8px unit. Rows have 16px padding, columns 24 to 48px gaps, sections 40 to 48px apart.
    density: Medium. Roomy rows of about 72px, read top to bottom like a report.
    corners: 4px on buttons and fields only. Lists and figures have no boxes.
    borders: A 2px ink rule opens the figures and the style sheet, a 1px ink rule sits under each section title, and 1px warm hairlines divide rows.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Thin 1.6px outline icons at 18px for search, bell and plus. Status
        marks are solid shapes in the status colour beside the word, a
        circle for On track, a triangle for At risk and a square with a
        white cross for Behind.
    focus: A 2px navy outline offset 3px. Fields get a navy border plus a 1px navy ring. A focused list row gets a 2px navy outline.
    tone: Measured full sentences, such as Good morning, Mara and Everything else is moving.
